      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Inheritance tax (IHT) in the UK can apply to assets, including those held offshore. However, the UK has reciprocal arrangements with some countries to avoid double taxation. To lawfully deal with unreported assets, they must be disclosed to HM Revenue and Customs (HMRC). It's critical for your client to accurately report all worldwide assets to avoid potential penalties or a retroactive IHT charge for previous years. Tax planning can be complex in such cases, and it's advisable to consult with a tax advisor or estate planner who has experience with international assets and situations.",
